      "effective_specification": {
        "task": {
          "solution_goal": "global_minimization",
          "code": "single_objective_optimization",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "Solve $\\min_{x\\in Q} f(x)$ using stochastic gradient responses queried inside $Q$. At a fixed query budget, minimize the worst-case expected objective gap of the returned feasible point."
          ],
          "navigation_domains": [
            "single_objective"
          ],
          "formulation_code": "SO.global_minimization"
        },
        "model": {
          "properties": {
            "convexity": "quasar_convex",
            "regularity": [
              "gradient_lipschitz"
            ],
            "structure": [],
            "growth": []
          },
          "domain_roles": {
            "function": "$\\mathbb R^d$",
            "optimization": "$Q$",
            "query": "$Q$",
            "output": "$Q$"
          },
          "code": "admissible_model_class",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "The public feasible set is the Euclidean ball $Q=B_2(0,D)=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\|x\\|_2\\le D\\}$. The unknown differentiable $f:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R$ has an $L$-Lipschitz gradient on the full space. At least one global minimizer is in $Q$, and the set $S=\\arg\\min_{x\\in Q} f(x)$ is convex.",
            "For all $x\\in Q$, let $p_S(x)$ be the Euclidean projection onto the minimizer set. The model requires",
            "$$\\tau(f(x)-f_*)\\le \\langle\\nabla f(x),x-p_S(x)\\rangle.$$",
            "The projection onto the hidden minimizer set defines quasar-convexity and is used in analysis. Only the projection onto the public ball is an available operation."
          ],
          "geometry_refs": [
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__ambient",
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__ball"
          ]
        },
        "oracle": {
          "code": "fresh_stochastic_gradient",
          "domain": "$Q$",
          "variant": "fresh_unbiased_bounded_variance_gradient",
          "public_inputs": [
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__p_d",
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__p_L",
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__p_D",
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__p_tau",
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__p_sigma",
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__p_T",
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__public_ball"
          ],
          "hidden_objects": [
            "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__f"
          ],
          "operations": [
            {
              "id": "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__fresh_gradient",
              "operation_code": "fresh_stochastic_gradient",
              "target_object": "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__f",
              "domain_ref": "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__ball",
              "query_signature": "$x\\in Q$",
              "response_signature": "$g(x;\\xi)\\in\\mathbb R^d$",
              "derivative_order": "first",
              "feedback_quality": {
                "code": "stochastic_unbiased"
              },
              "coupling": "One fresh independent draw per response. There is no sample handle or scalar function value.",
              "cost_rule_ref": "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__gradient_cost"
            }
          ],
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "Each call at $x\\in Q$ returns a single full stochastic gradient $g(x;\\xi)\\in\\mathbb R^d$. Conditional on the query and past, $\\mathbb E[g(x;\\xi)]=\\nabla f(x)$ and $\\mathbb E\\|g(x;\\xi)-\\nabla f(x)\\|_2^2\\le\\sigma^2$.",
            "The oracle law is fixed before interaction. Each call uses fresh independent randomness. There is no value feedback or sample handle. The learner can project onto $Q$ using its public center and radius."
          ]
        },
        "output": {
          "domain": "$Q$",
          "code": "output_space",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "Return a feasible point $\\widehat x\\in Q$. Any measurable feasible postprocessing is allowed, including an unqueried point, random iterate or convex combination. No function value or certificate is required."
          ]
        },
        "metric": {
          "code": "objective_gap",
          "formula_latex": "f(\\widehat x)-f_*\\,,\\qquad f_*=\\min_{x\\in Q} f(x)",
          "base_expression": "f(\\widehat x)-f_*\\,,\\qquad f_*=\\min_{x\\in Q} f(x)",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "Evaluate the unnormalized loss $f(\\widehat x)-f_*\\,,\\qquad f_*=\\min_{x\\in Q} f(x)$. It is finite and nonnegative. The minimizer promise means $f_*$ also equals the full-space minimum."
          ]
        },
        "resource": {
          "unit": "One full stochastic-gradient response",
          "budget_mode": "fixed_worst_case",
          "accounting": {
            "atomic_unit": "One full stochastic-gradient response",
            "budget_mode": "fixed_worst_case",
            "arithmetic_precision": "exact_real_unpriced_unless_specified",
            "free_operations": "Public ball projection, internal arithmetic, and storage on available information."
          },
          "code": "oracle_resource",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "Every full response costs one call, including all responses to batch queries. The cap is $N\\le T$ on every run. Internal computation, storage and projection onto $Q$ are free."
          ],
          "components": [
            {
              "code": "N_gradient",
              "unit": "call",
              "description": "One full fresh stochastic gradient response."
            }
          ],
          "cost_rules": [
            {
              "id": "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__gradient_cost",
              "operation_refs": [
                "SO_FO_QC_BALL_FRESH__main__fresh_gradient"
              ],
              "cost": {
